  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879798",
      "title": "Structuring Vuex Code & Files",
      "lectureOrder": 226,
      "videoOrder": 199,
      "sourceHash": "a58ab312848236b54aafccb7f615f088c56a717c906ff68709c076eb1f455ab6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 3.7,
          "en": "With that, we are almost done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.7,
          "end": 7.81,
          "en": "with the basics, but there is one, maybe obvious problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.81,
          "end": 10.32,
          "en": "the main JS file is huge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.32,
          "end": 14.12,
          "en": "It has the entire store and even an extra module in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.12,
          "end": 16.85,
          "en": "and it might work for this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.85,
          "end": 18.66,
          "en": "but even here, it's a lot of code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.66,
          "end": 19.56,
          "en": "In bigger apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.56,
          "end": 23.023,
          "en": "I definitely don't want to have that all in main JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.94,
          "end": 26.27,
          "en": "Instead, just as with rooting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.27,
          "end": 29.03,
          "en": "you typically create extra files for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.03,
          "end": 31.61,
          "en": "You could start with a store JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.61,
          "end": 34.82,
          "en": "and outsource your entire store into that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.82,
          "end": 37.07,
          "en": "That might be a good start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.07,
          "end": 41.02,
          "en": "So let's grab the module and this store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.02,
          "end": 45.863,
          "en": "cut it all from main JS and instead, add it in store JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.82,
          "end": 48.32,
          "en": "And then also, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.32,
          "end": 51.05,
          "en": "cut the create store import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.05,
          "end": 52.52,
          "en": "go to store JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.43,
          "end": 55.15,
          "en": "and add the import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.15,
          "end": 58.17,
          "en": "because we use create store in his file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.17,
          "end": 62.34,
          "en": "and then in the end, export the store as a default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.34,
          "end": 65.53,
          "en": "so that we can import it in main JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.53,
          "end": 68.94,
          "en": "Import store from store JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.97,
          "end": 72.47,
          "en": "and with that, everything should be working again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.33,
          "end": 76.57,
          "en": "Yes. But this is just a start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.57,
          "end": 81.2,
          "en": "Store JS is still huge and in bigger apps with many modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.2,
          "end": 83.873,
          "en": "this quickly becomes a super large file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.76,
          "end": 88.11,
          "en": "Therefore, typically, we go even further than that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.11,
          "end": 91.69,
          "en": "Often, you add a separate folder named store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.69,
          "end": 95.61,
          "en": "and in there, you then have your index JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.61,
          "end": 99.023,
          "en": "which holds your main store creation logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.88,
          "end": 104.88,
          "en": "then you have separate files for actions and mutations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.43,
          "end": 111.283,
          "en": "possibly all the for getters, if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.31,
          "end": 115.71000000000001,
          "en": "And then we create separate sub folders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.71000000000001,
          "end": 117.59,
          "en": "for all the modules we might have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.59,
          "end": 119.45,
          "en": "like the counter module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.45,
          "end": 122.09,
          "en": "And then there again, you could have a index JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.09,
          "end": 125.58,
          "en": "actions JS ends on to merge things together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.58,
          "end": 127.74,
          "en": "Now I'm going to split it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.74,
          "end": 129.89,
          "en": "to show you how this could work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.89,
          "end": 132.33,
          "en": "I will also be honest for this demo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.33,
          "end": 134.583,
          "en": "of course, that's all overkill.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.89,
          "end": 137.78,
          "en": "But with Deb, we have a bunch of files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.78,
          "end": 141.31,
          "en": "and now let's see how we split the code into those files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.31,
          "end": 143.44,
          "en": "In store JS here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.44,
          "end": 147.023,
          "en": "I will grab from my main store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.35,
          "end": 153.623,
          "en": "this whole logic to create a store, including the export.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.86,
          "end": 160.09,
          "en": "And I will cut that and add it to index JS in store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.09,
          "end": 163.653,
          "en": "So not index inside of counter, but index inside of store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.643,
          "end": 168.37,
          "en": "I'll also grab the import here of create store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.37,
          "end": 171.853,
          "en": "and add that to index JS in the store folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.42000000000002,
          "end": 176.66,
          "en": "Now, I grab my mutations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.66,
          "end": 180.093,
          "en": "in this case, the one root mutation I have here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.06,
          "end": 187.06,
          "en": "grab this object here and in the mutations JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 187.1,
          "end": 190.62,
          "en": "I will simply export this object now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 190.62,
          "end": 192.21,
          "en": "Again, this is overkill.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.21,
          "end": 194.36,
          "en": "Just having one object in a file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 194.36,
          "end": 197.56,
          "en": "there would be nothing wrong with having that in index JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 197.56,
          "end": 200.27,
          "en": "I'll just show you the ultimate solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 200.27,
          "end": 201.923,
          "en": "for very big apps here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.14,
          "end": 206.34,
          "en": "So with that, I'm exporting my mutation object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 206.34,
          "end": 209.66,
          "en": "and re-import that in index JS then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.66,
          "end": 214.66,
          "en": "Import mutations from mutations JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 216.823,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "Maybe also named as root mutations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 222.53,
          "en": "to make it clear that these are the mutations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.53,
          "end": 225.25,
          "en": "that influence our root state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 225.25,
          "end": 228.813,
          "en": "And I assign root mutations to mutations then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 230.41,
          "end": 232.079,
          "en": "Same for actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.079,
          "end": 235.45,
          "en": "You can grab the actions, object actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.45,
          "end": 239.14,
          "en": "go to the actions JS file in the store folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 239.14,
          "end": 243.48,
          "en": "export it as a default, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.48,
          "end": 245.24,
          "en": "and back in index JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 245.24,
          "end": 250.24,
          "en": "we then import the root actions from actions JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 253.707,
          "end": 257.7,
          "en": "And then assign root actions here to actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 260.3,
          "end": 261.56,
          "en": "At the same, if you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 261.56,
          "end": 263.823,
          "en": "for getters, grab the getters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 264.68,
          "end": 268.223,
          "en": "export them into getters JS file, like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 269.49,
          "end": 271.17,
          "en": "And back at index JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.17,
          "end": 276.17,
          "en": "I import my root getters from ./gettersjs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 279.61,
          "end": 282.193,
          "en": "and assigned root getters to getters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 284.53,
          "end": 286.7,
          "en": "And now, this is a very lean file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 286.7,
          "end": 289.093,
          "en": "The state stays in here by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 290.39,
          "end": 292.31,
          "en": "Now for the modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 292.31,
          "end": 295.023,
          "en": "In store JS, I still have the counter module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 296.38,
          "end": 298.67,
          "en": "I now grab this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 298.67,
          "end": 300.41,
          "en": "so that store JS is empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 300.41,
          "end": 303.13,
          "en": "and hence we can delete the file, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 303.13,
          "end": 305.95,
          "en": "and go to the counter folder in the store folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 305.95,
          "end": 308.513,
          "en": "and there, in index JS, I paste it in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 309.39,
          "end": 311.54,
          "en": "And I export this entire object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 311.54,
          "end": 313.833,
          "en": "as a default simply like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 316.68,
          "end": 319.23,
          "en": "I leave namespaced here, I'll leave state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 319.23,
          "end": 321.65,
          "en": "but I grabbed the mutations object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 321.65,
          "end": 324.62,
          "en": "and move that to the mutations JS folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 324.62,
          "end": 326.9,
          "en": "in this counter sub folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 326.9,
          "end": 329.66,
          "en": "and exports that in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 329.66,
          "end": 331.51,
          "en": "And then again, in index JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 331.51,
          "end": 334.89,
          "en": "but now in index JS inside of the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 334.89,
          "end": 339.89,
          "en": "I import counter mutations from ./mutationsjs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 342.6,
          "end": 346.463,
          "en": "and assign those here to mutations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 347.86,
          "end": 349.71,
          "en": "Same thing for actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 349.71,
          "end": 353.54,
          "en": "Grab the object, go to actions JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 353.54,
          "end": 355.953,
          "en": "export them here as a default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 357.55,
          "end": 362.55,
          "en": "like this, and in index JS, import them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 363.32,
          "end": 368.32,
          "en": "Import counter actions from actions JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 368.73,
          "end": 371.063,
          "en": "and assign them here to actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 373,
          "end": 373.91,
          "en": "And last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 373.91,
          "end": 377.24,
          "en": "we can do the same thing here for getters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 377.24,
          "end": 379.2,
          "en": "Grab the getters object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 379.2,
          "end": 382.323,
          "en": "add a getters JS file inside of the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 383.27,
          "end": 385.983,
          "en": "export our getters object like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 387.37,
          "end": 388.793,
          "en": "and then import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 390.14,
          "end": 392.3,
          "en": "Of course, you can tweak the file names, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 392.3,
          "end": 394.9,
          "en": "you don't have to use these exact file names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 394.9,
          "end": 397.07,
          "en": "I'm just following some convention here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 397.07,
          "end": 399.57,
          "en": "but you could also use a different file name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 401.2,
          "end": 406.2,
          "en": "So here I then have to counter getters from getters JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 408.45,
          "end": 409.963,
          "en": "So I'll assign them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 411.15999999999997,
          "end": 413.37,
          "en": "And now, this all split up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 413.37,
          "end": 415.2,
          "en": "I'm exporting my module here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 415.2,
          "end": 418.73,
          "en": "so now in index JS here, in the store folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 418.73,
          "end": 422.49,
          "en": "I can import my counter module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 422.49,
          "end": 427.43,
          "en": "from counter index JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 427.43,
          "end": 431.473,
          "en": "And now assign my counter module to numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 433.65,
          "end": 438.45,
          "en": "And now in main JS, we no longer import store from store JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 438.45,
          "end": 442.003,
          "en": "but from the store folder enter there the index JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 443.84,
          "end": 448.43,
          "en": "And with all that out of the way, it works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 448.43,
          "end": 451.23,
          "en": "but now with a different folder structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 451.23,
          "end": 453.68,
          "en": "Now, if you want that structure, know that it's up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 453.68,
          "end": 455.76,
          "en": "but it is one option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 455.76,
          "end": 457.34000000000003,
          "en": "You can also change this a bit more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 457.34000000000003,
          "end": 459.28,
          "en": "If you had multiple modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 459.28,
          "end": 461.88,
          "en": "you could also add a modules folder here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 461.88,
          "end": 464.94,
          "en": "and move counter into modules",
